1
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,530
It might be inappropriate

2
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:16,030
[It might be inappropriate of me to say this
when I made a mistake yesterday...]

3
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,780
of me to say this
when I made a mistake yesterday...

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:17,820
But can you promise me one thing?

5
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:18,290
[But can you promise me one thing?]

6
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:20,420
What?

7
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:27,240
[No matter what happens in the future,
don't get hurt, you fool.]

8
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:26,430
No matter what happens in the future,
don't get hurt,

9
00:00:26,430 --> 00:00:27,500
you fool.

10
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:34,200
[Promise me.]

11
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:33,950
Promise me.

12
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,220
I promise you.

13
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:44,750
As long as you stay by my side,

14
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,640
I won't let anyone get hurt.

15
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,500
Promise.

16
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:55,930
But

17
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:59,970
you're already covered in scars
because of me.

18
00:01:13,789 --> 00:01:20,370
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

19
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:26,320
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

20
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,110
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

21
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:32,020
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

22
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:50,220
[Yoo Dohyun]

23
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,680
[Cho Chanhyeon]

24
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:53,370
[Ko Gyeol]

25
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:58,360
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

26
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:04,950
Hanyul.

27
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:08,889
Here.

28
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,980
This is a wild river eel
found only deep in Jirisan.

29
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,570
I heard you have to boil it
without anything to get a thick broth,

30
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:14,900
so I put the whole eel in.

31
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,540
Try it.

32
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,950
Ah, is it too big?

33
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,040
I'll cut it up for you.

34
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:32,950
This is bat bile found only
in the high mountains of the Himalayas.

35
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,710
So bitter.

36
00:02:44,829 --> 00:02:45,760
Damn it.

37
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:47,240
What are you doing?

38
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,140
Hey, fire! Fire!

39
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:50,610
Fire! Fire...

40
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:54,560
Water! It's a flood! Damn it!

41
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:56,210
Seriously, Lee Won?

42
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,090
I originally wanted to

43
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,350
just build a fountain,

44
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:18,750
but I was afraid of being scolded by Pan,
so I held it back.

45
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,300
They say you have to sleep
in a humid environment

46
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,160
so your vocal cords
can recover as soon as possible.

47
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,210
Come on.

48
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,940
Make a wish quickly.

49
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:33,170
Please let Lee Hanyul's voice recover
as soon as possible.

50
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:37,090
Hey, you make a wish too.

51
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:42,000
Hey, why aren't you making a wish?

52
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:45,750
Ah.

53
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:47,530
You can't speak.

54
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:49,610
Are you stupid?

55
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,590
Yeah, I am stupid.

56
00:03:54,990 --> 00:03:57,770
So until your voice goes back to normal,

57
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,810
I'll continue to be stupid.

58
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:02,750
Make a wish.

59
00:04:27,090 --> 00:04:28,290
What! What happened!

60
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,500
Damn it, who is it!

61
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,530
What is all this?

62
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,680
I heard this is the best
for reducing swelling,

63
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,850
so I took a bath with
the highest grade herbal concentrate.

64
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:38,550
Maybe there's a hole in the tub.

65
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:40,350
I was taking a half-body bath...

66
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,070
You, wait a minute.

67
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,200
I thought you were dead!

68
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,130
Hey.

69
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,060
Hanyul, you... you spoke!

70
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:48,070
Oh?

71
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:50,920
You spoke!

72
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:51,740
I spoke!

73
00:04:51,870 --> 00:04:52,870
You spoke!

74
00:04:53,110 --> 00:04:54,100
-You spoke!
-I spoke!

75
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:57,090
You spoke! You have a voice!

76
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,320
Ah, ah.

77
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,460
But it's really a blessing, isn't it?

78
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:05,020
Hey.

79
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:09,270
Lee Won has done so much for you.

80
00:05:09,430 --> 00:05:11,000
With his sincerity,

81
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:13,970
even the carrots
in the fridge might start talking.

82
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,650
I'm suddenly curious if carrots can talk.

83
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,710
You just want to eat carrots, don't you?

84
00:05:20,710 --> 00:05:21,670
Yeah.

85
00:05:28,610 --> 00:05:31,710
[Lee Won, I hope your voice recovers soon.
I have something I really want to give you.]

86
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:33,690
By the way, where is Lee Won?

87
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,510
Secretary Kim said

88
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:40,020
he hasn't been to work for days
and has been holed up in his room.

89
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,440
Could he be composing?

90
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:52,350
[My voice is...]

91
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,690
I'm going out for a bit.

92
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:56,520
Hey, finish eating before you go.

93
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,420
Hey!

94
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,010
You're leaving them...

95
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,030
Oh.

96
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,420
You're here.

97
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,890
I was just about to go look for you.

98
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:09,760
Here.

99
00:06:09,930 --> 00:06:10,940
It's yours.

100
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,960
I finally finished writing it.

101
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,530
A song for you.

102
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,970
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

103
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,300
Oh.

104
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:24,790
Why did you come to my house?

105
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,630
I can speak now.

106
00:06:29,810 --> 00:06:30,920
Seriously?

107
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:31,730
Yeah.

108
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:32,760
Listen.

109
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:37,370
Lee Won, I can speak now!

110
00:06:42,930 --> 00:06:44,260
That's great.

111
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:46,700
That's really great.

112
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:58,750
By the way, what is this? Mine?

113
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:00,980
Yeah, yours.

114
00:07:06,650 --> 00:07:08,550
You need to warm up your voice first.

115
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:10,810
After all, you haven't used it
in a while.

116
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:14,490
Okay, let's go to the piano...

117
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,280
What are you doing in broad daylight?

118
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,670
What else? Practicing scales.

119
00:07:21,970 --> 00:07:23,390
Here?

120
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,610
There's an instrument here,

121
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,510
and I'm in charge of playing it.

122
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:31,070
Do you need anything else?

123
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,220
What nonsense are you talking about?

124
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:07,200
So don't hold back your voice, Hanyul.

125
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,880
I've already warmed up my voice.

126
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:23,020
Let's stop here.

127
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:26,520
By the way,

128
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,930
why did you suddenly give me a song?

129
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:32,929
-Could it be...
-Yeah.

130
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,980
You're going to debut.

131
00:08:35,039 --> 00:08:36,370
Really?

132
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:49,830
[Park Hanhoo's Manager]

133
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:56,370
[Park Hanhoo's Manager]
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

134
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:11,440
[Park Hanhoo's Manager]

135
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:22,790
Who could be so good at vocal training?

136
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:27,380
I truly... admire myself too.

137
00:09:40,290 --> 00:09:43,490
Judas's "Afternoon Rock and Roll."

138
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,410
Today's special surprise guest is

139
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:50,150
the one sweeping
the national music charts.

140
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:53,230
Singing the OST
for "Park Hanhoo's Manager,"

141
00:09:53,350 --> 00:09:57,180
the eardrum boyfriend whose heavenly voice
melts the public's eardrums—

142
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:59,040
is Yul!

143
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:03,760
We really had a hard time inviting him.

144
00:10:03,830 --> 00:10:06,630
The listener message board
has already exploded.

145
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:10,590
Yeah, just hearing his voice
makes you think he must be super handsome.

146
00:10:10,590 --> 00:10:13,700
Even though he's a faceless singer,
it feels like you can see his face.

147
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:17,680
We can see him right now.

148
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:19,410
Are you all jealous?

149
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:22,730
I should say, just looking at him
makes you feel very satisfied.

150
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:24,590
Did you give birth to him, Samuel?

151
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,810
Yeah, I even want to say
I gave birth to him.

152
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:29,720
In my opinion,
if you say you gave birth to him,

153
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:33,200
there's absolutely
no resemblance in appearance.

154
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:35,010
Alright, enough with the jokes.

155
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:37,720
Yul, you debuted as a faceless singer.

156
00:10:37,850 --> 00:10:41,320
Is there any special reason
you chose not to reveal your face?

157
00:10:42,590 --> 00:10:47,010
I just hope the public
can hear my voice first.

158
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:50,390
I just want to keep everyone company
with my singing.

159
00:10:50,910 --> 00:10:54,140
We actually want to focus more
on your face.

160
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:57,190
We just want to focus on your face.

161
00:10:57,550 --> 00:10:58,760
Well.

162
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:02,290
Then I'll start asking the question
everyone's most curious about.

163
00:11:02,290 --> 00:11:06,770
We heard you didn't do music before,
but worked in other industries.

164
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:11,150
So what was the reason, and how
did you get the chance to sing this song?

165
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:18,540
-Really?
-Yeah.

166
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:21,110
Hanyul, thank you
for your hard work today.

167
00:11:21,330 --> 00:11:22,610
Thank you for coming to my show.

168
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:23,850
-Thank you.
-You really did a great job.

169
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:25,510
We have things to wrap up,

170
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:27,350
so we'll only leave later.

171
00:11:27,570 --> 00:11:28,320
Thank you.

172
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:29,340
-Good job.
-Take care.

173
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:30,550
Thank you.

174
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,600
Take care.

175
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:40,640
Aren't you a faceless singer?

176
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,950
You contacted Dawn Entertainment, right?

177
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,910
You know Pan
and Michelo don't get along,

178
00:11:52,310 --> 00:11:54,010
so you wanted to mess with us.

179
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:57,320
I'm not quite sure
what you're talking about.

180
00:11:57,630 --> 00:12:02,280
I don't know either Pan or Michelo.

181
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,140
I just want you to become
popular as soon as possible.

182
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,270
You don't know them?

183
00:12:07,570 --> 00:12:08,740
Really?

184
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,100
Yeah.

185
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:14,100
You really are easily misunderstood.

186
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,860
You had nothing to do
with Dawn Entertainment.

187
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:21,020
And you had nothing to do
with Adolph either.

188
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,390
You must feel very wronged.

189
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,510
Right?

190
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:33,290
Lee Hanyul,
how many times do I have to say this?

191
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,670
I really didn't kill Adolph.

192
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,970
Really?

193
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,770
I guess.

194
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:45,560
Adolph

195
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:49,990
is still alive.

196
00:12:56,850 --> 00:13:00,810
I didn't dare
let you see Adolph who won't wake up.

197
00:13:01,430 --> 00:13:04,620
But I thought if I kept him this way,

198
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:10,570
you might look at me differently.

199
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:18,240
I did have evil thoughts.

200
00:13:20,990 --> 00:13:22,360
But I...

201
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,630
What's wrong?

202
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,390
Adolph...

203
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,100
is gone.

204
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:36,400
What did you say?

205
00:13:41,810 --> 00:13:43,040
It's true!

206
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,240
I really have been taking care of him!

207
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,740
Why on earth do you have to go this far?

208
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:50,100
Using the excuse of Adolph who's dead—

209
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:52,030
what exactly do you want to do to me?

210
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:54,610
Will you only stop when you see me dead?

211
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:55,690
Is that it?

212
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:07,270
Adolph is not dead.

213
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:09,790
I thought when he wakes up,
I'll find you...

214
00:14:11,530 --> 00:14:12,500
Here.

215
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:16,000
Are you satisfied now?

216
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:19,770
You didn't just kill Adolph that day.

217
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:22,030
You killed me too.

218
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,470
Who are you?

219
00:14:33,070 --> 00:14:34,340
Just kill me.

220
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:36,200
I'm telling you to just kill me!

221
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:49,940
[Sound of Dawn]

222
00:14:59,850 --> 00:15:00,940
Hanyul!

223
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:07,760
I was planning to have a beer alone.
Want to join?

224
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:08,640
Sure.

225
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:12,670
How does it feel to officially debut?

226
00:15:13,630 --> 00:15:14,870
Just so-so.

227
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:16,290
You must be a little dazed.

228
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,550
With the sudden surge in popularity too.

229
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:21,730
I just wonder if I'm qualified enough.

230
00:15:21,730 --> 00:15:23,810
Huh? Why?

231
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:28,370
You absolutely deserve to be loved.

232
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,430
I might not be a good person.

233
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:35,650
No one is perfect from beginning to end.

234
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:38,850
Everyone has a little bit
of badness in them.

235
00:15:39,470 --> 00:15:43,050
Instead, those who claim
to be super nice people

236
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:45,310
are the ones you should be more wary of.

237
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:48,650
Oh, right.

238
00:15:48,850 --> 00:15:52,770
I heard you and Herod
have been good friends since high school.

239
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:58,360
Just now, I could tell
he seems to like you a lot.

240
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:11,290
Seems like he must've done
something gravely wrong to you.

241
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:15,750
But, Hanyul,

242
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:19,350
although I don't know what exactly it is,

243
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:22,720
he probably didn't have
any bad intentions.

244
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:28,730
He is indeed selfish and values
his own feelings the most in the world.

245
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:36,260
Actually, all of us members

246
00:16:36,510 --> 00:16:39,690
owe him our lives.

247
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,020
Owe him?

248
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:49,030
Back then, Saul's family
was in a bad financial situation,

249
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:51,620
and he got involved
with a bunch of shady jerks

250
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:53,640
and became completely depraved.

251
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:56,000
The one who risked his life
to get him out,

252
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,910
paid for his medical treatment,
and made him a decent person,

253
00:16:57,910 --> 00:16:59,070
was Herod.

254
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:02,780
The one who helped Samuel's family
pay off their debts

255
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:05,839
and let him pick up
the drumsticks again was also Herod.

256
00:17:06,589 --> 00:17:10,280
As for me, when I had nowhere

257
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,660
and was wandering around
on the Han River Bridge,

258
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:15,800
he grabbed me by the collar
and pulled me down.

259
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:21,339
In other people's eyes,
he might be a cold-blooded bastard,

260
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:25,819
but to us, he is our only salvation.

261
00:17:27,099 --> 00:17:31,090
He did so much,
yet never mentioned his own difficulties.

262
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:32,800
He's just a fool.

263
00:17:34,210 --> 00:17:35,980
Anyway, what I mean is,

264
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,170
what he did to you

265
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:40,740
might look like a mess at first glance,

266
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,620
but deep down,
it probably isn't like that.

267
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:51,360
I don't even know
what happened between you two,

268
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,470
and here I am rambling off.

269
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:57,060
I'm sorry for saying all this
when I don't even know your story.

